The filings only partly answer this question.

The filing gives a size measure for fiscal 2025 but no growth or performance trend. E-commerce net sales were approximately 7% of total net sales in 2025. [1] It also reports that digitally-enabled sales (sales initiated through a digital device, plus Costco Travel) were approximately 10% of total net sales in 2025. [1] The filing describes e-commerce as giving members convenience and a broader selection of goods and services. [1]

On context, the filing notes that comparable sales include sales from e-commerce sites operating for more than one year. [2] It also warns that e-commerce operations depend heavily on logistics providers and are negatively affected when services are not provided in a timely fashion. [3]

Missing from these passages are e-commerce sales growth rates, dollar amounts, prior-year comparisons, and profitability.